./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-auto-fit-codex.err:370:./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-codex.out:3:KEYBOARD: Add `interactive-widget=resizes-content` to the viewport meta as progressive enhancement, but do not depend on it alone. Drive `--app-vh` from `window.visualViewport.height` and account for `visualViewport.offsetTop`; listen to both `resize` and `scroll`, batch updates with `requestAnimationFrame`, and set the root shell to `height: var(--app-vh, 100dvh); overflow:hidden`. Use `100dvh` as fallback, not `100vh` or inherited `height:100%`. Detect keyboard-open approximately when `innerHeight - visualViewport.height > 120px` while the command input is focused. In that state hide the thumb row and terminal toolbar, compact the header, remove stage padding, and immediately refit the grid/NAWS. Call `input.scrollIntoView({block:"nearest"})` only after focus if its bounding rect is outside the visual viewport; do not force-scroll the page on every focus. `visualViewport` exposes the viewport actually visible after zoom/keyboard changes, while the Virtual Keyboard API remains limited availability, so it should not be the primary path. [Visual Viewport](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/VisualViewport), [Virtual Keyboard API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/VirtualKeyboard_API)
