./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-auto-fit-codex.err:637:./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-codex.err:2654:KEYBOARD: Add `interactive-widget=resizes-content` to the viewport meta as progressive enhancement, but do not depend on it alone. Drive `--app-vh` from `window.visualViewport.height` and account for `visualViewport.offsetTop`; listen to both `resize` and `scroll`, batch updates with `requestAnimationFrame`, and set the root shell to `height: var(--app-vh, 100dvh); overflow:hidden`. Use `100dvh` as fallback, not `100vh` or inherited `height:100%`. Detect keyboard-open approximately when `innerHeight - visualViewport.height > 120px` while the command input is focused. In that state hide the thumb row and terminal toolbar, compact the header, remove stage padding, and immediately refit the grid/NAWS. Call `input.scrollIntoView({block:"nearest"})` only after focus if its bounding rect is outside the visual viewport; do not force-scroll the page on every focus. `visualViewport` exposes the viewport actually visible after zoom/keyboard changes, while the Virtual Keyboard API remains limited availability, so it should not be the primary path. [Visual Viewport](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/VisualViewport), [Virtual Keyboard API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/VirtualKeyboard_API)
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-auto-fit-codex.err:638:./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-codex.err:2666:4. In `apps/web/src/TerminalHost.tsx` and `lib/termFit.ts`, refit on every actual wrapper resize and visual-viewport transition, debounce NAWS until geometry settles, and remove the dangerous effective overflow caused by clamping to `minRows:12` when fewer than 12 rows physically fit. The reported grid must never be larger than the canvas area; permit a temporary 4–6-row emergency grid with the keyboard open.
