./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-hetero.md:15:1. **Shell height = `visualViewport`**, CSS var (`--app-vh` / `--vvh`), fallback `100dvh` — never bare `100vh` / `height:100%` alone for keyboard.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-hetero.md:19:5. **Do not CSS-scale canvas** — refit cell grid + NAWS; measured cols/rows must not exceed stage (no minRows inflate).
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-hetero.md:34:- `useVisualViewport` → `--app-vh`, `.kb-open`
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-hetero.md:38:- TerminalHost: compact mobile toolbar; VV resize listener
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-codex.out:3:KEYBOARD: Add `interactive-widget=resizes-content` to the viewport meta as progressive enhancement, but do not depend on it alone. Drive `--app-vh` from `window.visualViewport.height` and account for `visualViewport.offsetTop`; listen to both `resize` and `scroll`, batch updates with `requestAnimationFrame`, and set the root shell to `height: var(--app-vh, 100dvh); overflow:hidden`. Use `100dvh` as fallback, not `100vh` or inherited `height:100%`. Detect keyboard-open approximately when `innerHeight - visualViewport.height > 120px` while the command input is focused. In that state hide the thumb row and terminal toolbar, compact the header, remove stage padding, and immediately refit the grid/NAWS. Call `input.scrollIntoView({block:"nearest"})` only after focus if its bounding rect is outside the visual viewport; do not force-scroll the page on every focus. `visualViewport` exposes the viewport actually visible after zoom/keyboard changes, while the Virtual Keyboard API remains limited availability, so it should not be the primary path. [Visual Viewport](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/VisualViewport), [Virtual Keyboard API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/VirtualKeyboard_API)
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-codex.out:9:MOVEMENT: Keep the six chips for portrait keyboard-closed, but make them one non-wrapping 44px-high horizontal row; wrapping is the current vertical-space failure. Put `n/s/e/w` first and allow `look/score/map` to scroll horizontally. Hide that row while the soft keyboard is open. Do not use a 3×3 D-pad below the command bar in portrait—it costs roughly 136–152px. Do not make canvas swipe the only movement method because it conflicts with scrollback, selection, map interaction, and accidental combat movement. In landscape, use a compact 3×3 D-pad or four-way side rail outside the canvas; optional canvas swipe may be opt-in, require a clear 40–50px gesture, and provide visual confirmation.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-codex.out:13:2. In `apps/web/src/styles/tokens.css` and `index.css`, replace the `html, body, #root { height:100% }` dependency with `--app-vh`, `100dvh` fallback, `overflow:hidden`, mobile `--topbar-h/--cmd-h` tokens, safe-area handling, and portrait/short-landscape media queries.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-codex.out:15:4. In `apps/web/src/TerminalHost.tsx` and `lib/termFit.ts`, refit on every actual wrapper resize and visual-viewport transition, debounce NAWS until geometry settles, and remove the dangerous effective overflow caused by clamping to `minRows:12` when fewer than 12 rows physically fit. The reported grid must never be larger than the canvas area; permit a temporary 4–6-row emergency grid with the keyboard open.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-codex.out:16:5. In `App.tsx` footer and `TerminalHost.tsx` toolbar, make chips non-wrapping, reduce Send width, hide the thumb row during keyboard entry, replace the three always-visible copy buttons with one 44px overflow/copy action on small screens, and add the portrait-only landscape-play control with CSS fallback.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-codex.out:19:- Never CSS-scale the canvas to fit a desired 80×24 grid; resize the backing grid and send the real cols×rows through NAWS.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-codex.out:26:- Never send continuous NAWS updates for every noisy viewport pixel; coalesce and send only changed stable cell geometry.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-agy.out:13:  - Terminal Stage (Flex 1 / ~70–75%): Recalculates rows via NAWS (~12–16 rows × 80 cols).
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-agy.out:17:- Viewport & Resize API: Use `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, interactive-widget=resizes-content">` for modern Android Chrome. For iOS WebKit (where `100vh`/`100dvh` fail with keyboard up), listen to `window.visualViewport.addEventListener('resize', ...)` and update `--vv-height: ${window.visualViewport.height}px` on document root. App root uses `height: var(--vv-height, 100dvh)`.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-agy.out:20:- Terminal Recalculation: Debounce `window.visualViewport` resize events (via `requestAnimationFrame`) to re-trigger terminal cell fit and dispatch updated NAWS telnet signal (`cols`, `rows`).
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-agy.out:25:  - Left Stage (80% width / Flex 1): Full-height Canvas2D terminal stage maximizing NAWS cols (80–120+ cols × 24–30 rows).
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-agy.out:41:2. `TerminalHost.tsx` / `fit.ts`: Calculate Canvas HTML element width/height using exact integer multiples of cell dimensions (`cols * cellWidth`, `rows * cellHeight`) updated on `visualViewport` resize. Never rely on CSS `width: 100%` canvas stretch.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-agy.out:43:4. `tokens.css` / `layout.css`: Define dynamic `--vv-height` bound to `window.visualViewport.height`, and enforce `position: fixed; overflow: hidden;` on body/html root.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-agy.out:53:ONE_LINE: Bind container height to `visualViewport` JS events, auto-hide movement chrome during keyboard focus, and preserve crisp Big5 MUD rendering via integer cell grid fitting in an 80/20 landscape split view.
