./docs/reviews/phase1a-r3-minimax.json.raw:3:{ "runner": "anthropic-compatible", "model": "MiniMax-M3", "status": "reviewed", "verdict": "FIX-THEN-SHIP", "findings": "- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:isPrivateOrBlockedIp — IPv6 ULA check only matches `fc/fd/fe80:` prefixes without proper colon boundaries; `fcd` or `fcaa` style matches would falsely block public IPv6 (e.g. anything starting `fc` in the first hextet is fine, but the prefix check lacks length validation so a 1-char host like `fc` passes through incorrectly; minor but logically weak).\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:checkAuth — Query-string token accepted even in remote-prod mode defeats the Bearer/cookie preference stated in comment; token in URL leaks via server logs/referrer and is a known web vuln (still documented as \"local smoke\" but prod has no guard).\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:assertDestinationAllowed — `loopbackAllow` allows `127.0.0.1`/`localhost` only in localhost-dev mode even when host is on allowlist; in remote-prod the allowlist may contain `127.0.0.1` entry but it's still blocked, which may or may not be intended (not a defect, just ambiguity — accept).\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:assertDestinationAllowed — DNS result is validated against private ranges but there is no TOCTOU re-check pinning at TCP connect time; server.ts does pass `dest.address` (good), but if DNS changes between lookup and connect, Node's `net.connect({host})` will re-resolve — verify `bridge.ts` uses the literal IP (it does: `host: opts.host` which is `dest.address`). OK.\n- apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts — `sock.on(\"error\")` JSON message could include arbitrary text after sanitization but the close code `1011` leaks internal error to client; acceptable for proxy debug.\n- apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts — No size limit on incoming TCP data buffering before parser push; parser grows `this.buf` unbounded across pushes (`this.buf = merged`). A malicious MUD could send a very large un-terminated IAC SB to grow memory until OOM. Missing backpressure/cap.\n- apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts — `parser.push` accumulates all events into an array per chunk with `data` building via `number[]` array (slow for big5/UTF-8 streams); performance issue, not security.\n- apps/proxy/src/server.ts — `checkOrigin` rejects empty origin only in remote-prod; `localhost-dev` mode accepts any missing-origin request, which combined with `relaxAllowlist: true` allows CSRF from any non-browser context — acceptable for dev.\n- apps/proxy/src/server.ts — `assertDestinationAllowed` is called with the raw query `mudHost` (user-controlled) and the validated IP is used in `wss.handleUpgrade` callback only after `await` resolves; if client disconnects during await, socket may already be destroyed by client and `handleUpgrade` would fail silently (caught by outer try/catch — OK).\n- apps/proxy/tests/policy.test.ts — Tests use `prod` object spread from `defaultConfig(\"remote-prod\")` which has `relaxAllowlist: false` and `originAllowlist` from env (empty in tests), so test's `originAllowlist: [\"https://mud.example.com\"]` override is needed; minor test brittleness.\n- packages/protocol/src/telnet.ts — `TelnetParser.push` `this.buf = this.buf.slice(i)` keeps growing because slice copies; should compact. Memory leak under sustained malformed input.\n- packages/protocol/src/telnet.ts — No upper bound on SB payload size; a MUD sending a multi-MB subnegotiation without IAC SE will buffer forever. DoS.\n- packages/vt/src/sgr.ts:tokenizeAnsi — `params = body.split(\";\").filter(x => x.length && !x.startsWith(\"?\")).map(x => parseInt(x,10) || 0)` — empty param `;;` becomes `\"\"` filtered out, losing semantics (SGR empty params = 0). Subtle correctness bug.\n- packages/vt/src/sanitize.ts:sanitizeMudTextForHtml — Iterates with spread `[...text]` then joins; O(n) but fine. No defect.\n- packages/terminal/src/buffer.ts:lineFeed — Pushes to scrollback unconditionally even when `cursor.c === 0` and line is blank, polluting scrollback with empty strings.\n- packages/terminal/src/buffer.ts:writeDecoded — Other CSI (cursor positioning CUP, clear screen ED) silently ignored — Phase 1a partial terminal acknowledged in spec, not a defect.\n- apps/web/src/App.tsx — `token` stored in `localStorage` and sent as URL query param `?token=` which is logged by proxies and visible in Referer headers — security regression vs. Authorization header path.\n- apps/web/src/App.tsx — `host` and `port` are user-editable; client can attempt SSRF via proxy (proxy enforces allowlist, so safe).\n- apps/web/src/TerminalHost.tsx — `sendLine` sends raw `line` as text frame; bridge.ts handles text frames but rejects IAC bytes via `replace(/\\xff/g, \"\")` — OK. No length validation on input before send.\n- apps/web/src/TerminalHost.tsx — WS message handler does not validate `ev.data` is ArrayBuffer when binary — relies on `binaryType = \"arraybuffer\"`; if proxy sends Blob, would crash. Minor.\n- apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts — `sock.on(\"data\")` does not handle backpressure; if WS client is slow, `ws.send` queues in memory. Missing `ws.bufferedAmount` check or `drain` handling.\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:checkAuth — Cookie value decoded with `decodeURIComponent` then compared with safeEqual; no max length, no charset check — could match malformed cookie to token. Minor.\n- apps/proxy/src/server.ts — No `maxHeaderSize`, no `keepAliveTimeout` tuning; defaults are fine for proxy.\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:defaultConfig — `authToken` from env may be empty string and `!token` returns false so empty token = reject all — correct behavior but undocumented.\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:assertDestinationAllowed — `Number.isInteger(port)` rejects decimal ports from query (e.g. `port=4000.0`) — fine.\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:isPrivateOrBlockedIp — IPv4-mapped IPv6 recursion is fine but no recursion-depth guard; not exploitable.\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:checkOrigin — In remote-prod, exact string match on origin (good); but no normalization of trailing slash or default port. Minor.\n- apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts — `replyToNegotiation` returns `null` is not checked; `sendTcp` would be called with null. Wait: code is `if (reply) sendTcp(reply)` — OK.\n- apps/proxy/src/server.ts — No CSRF token on `/health`; it returns 200 but no sensitive data — OK.\n- apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts — `sock.on(\"close\")` closes WS with `1000` even if bridge closed due to client disconnect; acceptable.\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:safeEqual — Pads shorter string with null bytes (`0`); not strictly constant-time under all JS engines due to JIT, but adequate for this use.\n- packages/codec-big5/src/index.ts — `parts.push(this.pending, bytes[0]!)` — `bytes[0]` is always defined; the `!` suppresses. If `bytes.length === 0` early return handles it. OK.\n- packages/vt/src/sgr.ts — `applySgr` accepts `p >= 90 && p <= 97` (bright fg) but doesn't accept `p === 1` combined with bright in same sequence beyond what spec covers. OK.\n- apps/web/src/TerminalHost.tsx — `decoderRef.current.reset()` on unmount, but if WS is mid-message, decoder state is lost. Minor.\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:assertDestinationAllowed — `address === \"169.254.169.254\"` check happens after DNS lookup but before the private-IP generic check; redundant since `isPrivateOrBlockedIp(\"169.254.169.254\")` returns true. OK.\n- apps/proxy/src/server.ts — `import.meta` / dynamic env used in client (App.tsx) — not in server. OK.\n- apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts — `escapeIac` doubles IAC bytes (255 → 255 255) which is correct for telnet.\n- packages/protocol/src/telnet.ts:TelnetParser — `cmd` returned by `replyToNegotiation` is a `Uint8Array`; `sendTcp(Buffer.from(buf))` converts. OK.\n- apps/proxy/src/policy.ts:checkAuth — `decodeURIComponent` of cookie can throw on malformed `%` — caught. OK.", "raw_log": "/tmp/dispatch-review-log-TT9Cko", "error": null }
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-kimi.out:10:- Use window.visualViewport to set a CSS var --vvh (actual visual viewport height in px) on #root. All shell sizing should be based on --vvh, not 100vh or 100%.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-kimi.out:11:- In index.html add `interactive-widget=resizes-content` to the viewport meta for Android Chrome; iOS still needs visualViewport fallback.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-kimi.out:14:- On input focus call input.scrollIntoView({ block: "nearest" }); the visualViewport resize handler will refit the terminal within one frame.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-kimi.out:15:- Debounce the NAWS refit in TerminalHost on visualViewport resize.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-kimi.out:20:- Provide a CSS-only dual layout via `@media (orientation: landscape) and (max-height: 500px)`: hide the header and thumb pad, turn the command bar into a thin 48 dp strip (bottom or right edge), and let the terminal canvas fill the rest. Recompute NAWS to gain cols (aim for 90–120) rather than rows.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-kimi.out:36:2. apps/web/src/App.tsx (footer ~line 1713): drive shell height from visualViewport and hide the thumb-pad row while the command input has focus / keyboard is open.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-kimi.out:38:4. apps/web/src/TerminalHost.tsx (toolbar ~lines 656–726): collapse the copy/screen-history toolbar into a single "⋮ Copy" overflow menu on small screens; the current four-button row steals too much terminal space.
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-kimi.out:39:5. apps/web/src/lib/termFit.ts / TerminalHost: re-fit cols/rows on visualViewport resize, not just on layout ResizeObserver, and clamp to sensible mobile minimums (≥40 cols, ≥12 rows, but allow rows down to ~8 in keyboard-open portrait).
./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-kimi.out:48:- Don't resize the terminal solely based on the layout viewport; iOS needs visualViewport.
./docs/reviews/phase1a-minimax.json.raw:3:{ "runner": "anthropic-compatible", "model": "MiniMax-M3", "status": "reviewed", "verdict": "FIX-THEN-SHIP", "findings": "CRITICAL: apps/proxy/src/policy.ts assertDestinationAllowed returns the resolved IP via lookup() but server.ts uses dest.address only as a cosmetic ternary in bridge host while still passing mudHost to net.connect, so an attacker-controlled mudHost can be DNS-rebound to a private IP after the allowlist check — SSRF bypass. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts checkOrigin in localhost-dev mode accepts any origin starting with http://127.0.0.1 or http://localhost with no trailing slash match, so an origin like http://127.0.0.1.evil.com would pass (prefix match without boundary) — Origin bypass. MAJOR: apps/proxy/src/policy.ts isPrivateOrBlockedIp only blocks 169.254.169.254 explicitly inside the function for AWS metadata; 169.254.x link-local in general is blocked which is fine, but IPv6 private ranges (fc00::/7 unique-local, fe80::/10 link-local, ::ffff:0:0/96 IPv4-mapped) are entirely missing — IPv6 SSRF bypass via DNS AAAA. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts assertDestinationAllowed performs DNS lookup once but does not pin the address: net.connect in bridge.ts uses the original mudHost, and Node will re-resolve DNS, allowing TOCTOU DNS rebinding between policy check and connect. apps/proxy/src/server.ts:31 reads `req.headers.host` and constructs `new URL(req.url, \"http://\"+hostHdr)` without validating the Host header; in remote-prod bound to 0.0.0.0 this is acceptable but combined with the host-allowlist matching on user-supplied mudHost it should pin connect to dest.address, not mudHost. apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts ws.on(\"message\") sends raw client bytes to TCP socket with no length/rate limit; combined with `const s = String(data)` then appending \\r\\n for text frames, a client can inject IAC bytes (255) without escaping, breaking the telnet state machine on the mud side (IAC injection). apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts sock.on(\"data\") forwards parsed `ev.bytes` (application data only) — good for IAC — but on binary frames from the browser it passes isBinary=true to TextEncoder without normalizing; minor since proxy strips IAC. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts checkAuth reads cookie `assmud_session` and compares with `===` after decodeURIComponent; token echoed in URL `?token=` and `?auth=` is logged in any reverse-proxy access logs — token leakage via URL logging. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts isPrivateOrBlockedIp treats 0.0.0.0 as blocked which is good; however 100.64.0.0/10 (CGNAT) is not blocked, and 198.18.0.0/15 (benchmark) is not blocked — limited SSRF surface but should be addressed. apps/proxy/src/server.ts path check only allows `/ws` but does not reject query strings like `?host=` with embedded credentials that some MUDs use; minor. apps/proxy/src/server.ts response on origin/auth failures writes 403/401 but does not return a CORS preflight `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` — fine since origin check happens at WS upgrade, not CORS, but worth noting. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts originAllowlist exact-match comparison only; suffix attacks (e.g. `https://mud.example.com.evil.com`) correctly fail, good. MINOR: apps/proxy/src/policy.ts defaultConfig localhost-dev hardcodes 127.0.0.1:7788 with no env override; tests/dev users may conflict. apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts on ws.on(\"message\") converts text via TextEncoder then re-encodes via String() comparison; `const line = s.endsWith(\"\\n\") || s.endsWith(\"\\r\") ? s : s + \"\\r\\n\"` uses raw `s` (not the encoded form) for text frames, but `sendTcp` sends the TextEncoder-encoded version — semantically equivalent for ASCII but inconsistent; minor. apps/web/src/TerminalHost.tsx stores auth token in localStorage without any warning; web origin is the only protection. apps/web/src/main.tsx assigns Buffer to globalThis unconditionally; not a security issue per se. packages/codec-big5/src/index.ts Big5StreamDecoder uses iconv-lite 'big5hkscs'; correct for RW. packages/vt/src/sgr.ts tokenizeAnsi does not handle OSC sequences (ESC ]); could leak title strings to client but since output is drawn to canvas, no XSS risk — minor completeness. packages/terminal/src/buffer.ts scrollback stores plain strings (not cells with attrs); visible-color loss in scrollback — deferred per spec but worth noting. tsconfig.base.json noUnusedLocals may break build (e.g. apps/proxy/src/server.ts unused `WebSocketServer` types if any). vitest.config.ts environment is \"node\" globally; DOM-dependent code in apps/web would fail tests there but no web tests exist — fine. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts defaultConfig in dev mode includes `relaxAllowlist: true` allowing any public host; the dev-mode behavior still blocks private IPs which is correct. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts auth check accepts token via URL search param `?token=` — token ends up in browser history, server logs, referer headers; should prefer cookie/header only. apps/proxy/src/server.ts does not set a connection rate limit; DoS possible but acceptable for Phase 1a. apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts sock.write errors are not handled (only sock.on(\"error\")); minor. apps/proxy/src/server.ts uses `req.headers.origin` which can be empty string from same-origin; checkOrigin handles undefined but not \"\" — \"\" passes dev startsWith check, blocks prod via originAllowlist.includes(\"\") which is false — ok.", "raw_log": "/tmp/dispatch-review-log-RlZeN2", "error": null }
