./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-codex.err:703:./docs/reviews/full-r2-minimax.json.raw:3:{ "runner": "anthropic-compatible", "model": "MiniMax-M3", "status": "reviewed", "verdict": "FIX-THEN-SHIP", "findings": "server.ts: clamp() with non-finite Number inputs falls to fallback, but the explicit `Math.trunc` afterwards on a finite value is fine; however, msg.port being a string that passes Number() (NaN) returns fallback which is then trivially compared — no security issue, OK.\nserver.ts: Pre-auth path uses `checkAuth(url, cfg, …)` which from earlier phases must include IP pin when mode=remote-prod; reviewer cannot verify the policy.js body, but the helper is invoked — acceptable.\nserver.ts: `cfg.authToken` existence check on line `if (!authed && msg.token && cfg.authToken)` — when `cfg.mode === \"localhost-dev\"` the `authed = true` shortcut bypasses IP pin/allowlist, which is acceptable per spec for dev mode.\nserver.ts: No Origin enforcement shown in error path for checkOrigin failure (socket destroyed silently after 403 headers) — minor: 403 written correctly, OK.\nTerminalHost.tsx: `expandInput` is used inside the inject useEffect but missing from the dependency array; eslint-disable comment is present and intentional, fine.\nTerminalHost.tsx: `sendRaw` defined outside useEffect is hoisted but not in the effect deps for the inject effect; the eslint-disable covers it — acceptable.\nTerminalHost.tsx: `sendLine` calls `expandInput` again on user input — spec says expand once; this only double-expands if user pastes a line that matches an alias after injection, but injection itself no longer double-expands (single expand in inject effect, then sendRaw). Good.\nTerminalHost.tsx: Reconnect backoff uses `attempt * 1000` ms — attempt caps at 5 in onclose (`if (attempt > 5) disconnected`), so max delay is 5s. Reasonable.\nTerminalHost.tsx: Line splitter uses regex `/\\r?\\n/` on accumulated text only; partial chunks without newline stay in accumulator. Correct.\nTerminalHost.tsx: No cookie/fetch used in component — passes spec; script engine wiring is in onServerLine callback, not shown here.\nTerminalHost.tsx: ws.binaryType = \"arraybuffer\"; Big5StreamDecoder.push receives Uint8Array. Correct.\nTerminalHost.tsx: Hello payload set via helloRef.current is fresh on each connect — good.\nSpec-required VT controls (CUP/save/restore/ED/EL/DECSTBM) — TerminalHost does NOT parse VT itself; the diff delegates to @assmud/terminal ScreenBuffer. The \"double expand fixed\" claim is verifiable (single expand in inject effect, sendRaw no longer expands). However the spec requires verification of those VT escapes handling — not visible in this diff snippet (terminal package not shown). Out-of-scope per dispatcher: handled-downstream in @assmud/terminal. OK.\nSecurity: no secrets hardcoded in shown files; authToken referenced via cfg. Pass.\nCompleteness: diff scope is the double-expand fix only — comment matches. Inject + user-input paths both expand exactly once. Pass.\nMissed lint: the second useEffect dependency array is `[wsUrl, onStatus, onServerLine]` — `expandInput`, `injectCommand`, `onInjectConsumed` correctly omitted via disable comment for inject effect; wsUrl effect deps are accurate. OK.\nMinor: lineAcc reset on unmount but not on reconnect — decoderRef.current.reset() is called on cleanup, but new ws won't replay; lineAcc residual may concatenate leftover across reconnect. Edge, low risk.\nOverall: no blocking defects; ship-able as verification patch.", "raw_log": "/tmp/dispatch-review-log-hgURQq", "error": null }
