./docs/reviews/2026-07-22-mobile-ux-codex.err:983:./docs/reviews/phase1a-minimax.json.raw:3:{ "runner": "anthropic-compatible", "model": "MiniMax-M3", "status": "reviewed", "verdict": "FIX-THEN-SHIP", "findings": "CRITICAL: apps/proxy/src/policy.ts assertDestinationAllowed returns the resolved IP via lookup() but server.ts uses dest.address only as a cosmetic ternary in bridge host while still passing mudHost to net.connect, so an attacker-controlled mudHost can be DNS-rebound to a private IP after the allowlist check — SSRF bypass. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts checkOrigin in localhost-dev mode accepts any origin starting with http://127.0.0.1 or http://localhost with no trailing slash match, so an origin like http://127.0.0.1.evil.com would pass (prefix match without boundary) — Origin bypass. MAJOR: apps/proxy/src/policy.ts isPrivateOrBlockedIp only blocks 169.254.169.254 explicitly inside the function for AWS metadata; 169.254.x link-local in general is blocked which is fine, but IPv6 private ranges (fc00::/7 unique-local, fe80::/10 link-local, ::ffff:0:0/96 IPv4-mapped) are entirely missing — IPv6 SSRF bypass via DNS AAAA. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts assertDestinationAllowed performs DNS lookup once but does not pin the address: net.connect in bridge.ts uses the original mudHost, and Node will re-resolve DNS, allowing TOCTOU DNS rebinding between policy check and connect. apps/proxy/src/server.ts:31 reads `req.headers.host` and constructs `new URL(req.url, \"http://\"+hostHdr)` without validating the Host header; in remote-prod bound to 0.0.0.0 this is acceptable but combined with the host-allowlist matching on user-supplied mudHost it should pin connect to dest.address, not mudHost. apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts ws.on(\"message\") sends raw client bytes to TCP socket with no length/rate limit; combined with `const s = String(data)` then appending \\r\\n for text frames, a client can inject IAC bytes (255) without escaping, breaking the telnet state machine on the mud side (IAC injection). apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts sock.on(\"data\") forwards parsed `ev.bytes` (application data only) — good for IAC — but on binary frames from the browser it passes isBinary=true to TextEncoder without normalizing; minor since proxy strips IAC. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts checkAuth reads cookie `assmud_session` and compares with `===` after decodeURIComponent; token echoed in URL `?token=` and `?auth=` is logged in any reverse-proxy access logs — token leakage via URL logging. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts isPrivateOrBlockedIp treats 0.0.0.0 as blocked which is good; however 100.64.0.0/10 (CGNAT) is not blocked, and 198.18.0.0/15 (benchmark) is not blocked — limited SSRF surface but should be addressed. apps/proxy/src/server.ts path check only allows `/ws` but does not reject query strings like `?host=` with embedded credentials that some MUDs use; minor. apps/proxy/src/server.ts response on origin/auth failures writes 403/401 but does not return a CORS preflight `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` — fine since origin check happens at WS upgrade, not CORS, but worth noting. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts originAllowlist exact-match comparison only; suffix attacks (e.g. `https://mud.example.com.evil.com`) correctly fail, good. MINOR: apps/proxy/src/policy.ts defaultConfig localhost-dev hardcodes 127.0.0.1:7788 with no env override; tests/dev users may conflict. apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts on ws.on(\"message\") converts text via TextEncoder then re-encodes via String() comparison; `const line = s.endsWith(\"\\n\") || s.endsWith(\"\\r\") ? s : s + \"\\r\\n\"` uses raw `s` (not the encoded form) for text frames, but `sendTcp` sends the TextEncoder-encoded version — semantically equivalent for ASCII but inconsistent; minor. apps/web/src/TerminalHost.tsx stores auth token in localStorage without any warning; web origin is the only protection. apps/web/src/main.tsx assigns Buffer to globalThis unconditionally; not a security issue per se. packages/codec-big5/src/index.ts Big5StreamDecoder uses iconv-lite 'big5hkscs'; correct for RW. packages/vt/src/sgr.ts tokenizeAnsi does not handle OSC sequences (ESC ]); could leak title strings to client but since output is drawn to canvas, no XSS risk — minor completeness. packages/terminal/src/buffer.ts scrollback stores plain strings (not cells with attrs); visible-color loss in scrollback — deferred per spec but worth noting. tsconfig.base.json noUnusedLocals may break build (e.g. apps/proxy/src/server.ts unused `WebSocketServer` types if any). vitest.config.ts environment is \"node\" globally; DOM-dependent code in apps/web would fail tests there but no web tests exist — fine. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts defaultConfig in dev mode includes `relaxAllowlist: true` allowing any public host; the dev-mode behavior still blocks private IPs which is correct. apps/proxy/src/policy.ts auth check accepts token via URL search param `?token=` — token ends up in browser history, server logs, referer headers; should prefer cookie/header only. apps/proxy/src/server.ts does not set a connection rate limit; DoS possible but acceptable for Phase 1a. apps/proxy/src/bridge.ts sock.write errors are not handled (only sock.on(\"error\")); minor. apps/proxy/src/server.ts uses `req.headers.origin` which can be empty string from same-origin; checkOrigin handles undefined but not \"\" — \"\" passes dev startsWith check, blocks prod via originAllowlist.includes(\"\") which is false — ok.", "raw_log": "/tmp/dispatch-review-log-RlZeN2", "error": null }
